    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0183" n="861" sameAs="frus:frus1863p2/pg861"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr.
                        Taylor.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 18.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>,</placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >February</hi> 25, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of January 27 (No. 28) has
                    been received. I thank you most sincerely for the care you have so judiciously
                    bestowed upon the national cause, in translating for the department the article
                    in the Vedomosti, upon the President’s proclamation. It is a paper of marked
                    ability, candor, and foresight. I shall cause it to be published here.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bayard Taylor</hi>, Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
